From 3d5e01a18bfc2fde0db1ea9f5a46c9a8efd7a7e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Fix Darwin-only fixture failures in failed-result
 runtime, socket and replay tests

Native macOS run 43551929482 (job 132316188832, main 6825785665) failed three
platform-marked residuals that all pass on Linux:

1. tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_failed_result_runtime.py (26 cases):
   KeyError 'death_proof_version' in _hung_writer before any behaviour ran.
   Why: strict death proof requires valid_birth (a nonempty instantiation
   epoch), and current_instantiation_epoch() is empty off Linux, so real
   macOS fingerprints are "|<start>@<boottime>" and the writer never opts
   into the strict protocol. That is deliberate production policy: without
   a reboot-stable epoch a PID recycled across a reboot cannot be told apart,
   so production identity validation is unchanged. The tests model the
   protocol itself, so an autouse fixture pins one epoch (the host's real one
   on Linux, a fixture epoch elsewhere) in the parent and in the real writer
   child; processes, signals and finalizer assertions are unchanged. A new
   negative test forces an empty epoch on every POSIX host and proves the
   writer records no strict proof and expiry claims no verified death.

2. tests/gateway/test_control_socket_pause.py trickle test: AF_UNIX path too
   long under pytest's deep macOS tmp_path. Bind in a short mkdtemp root
   (short_home convention from test_shutdown_watchdog.py), cleaned up in
   finally; the real trickling peer and single deadline are unchanged.

3. tests/ci/test_update_ci_routing.py replay-python3 test: its bare child
   interpreter (no pytest) asserts when the host has no bash >= 4 (mini:
   /bin/bash 3.2), while every sibling replay test skips via replay_bash().
   Call the established replay_bash() selector in the pytest parent first so
   it shares that prerequisite skip; the child's minimal-PATH interpreter
   semantics are unchanged. Provisioning bash 4 on the runner is the sibling
   environment card's scope.

Test-only change; revert this commit to reverse.
